# ─── Apex Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: do NOT add a blanket `.apex-code/` rule.
#
# `<project>/.apex-code/` is the project-local config directory — extensions,
# prompts, skills, settings — and it is meant to be VERSIONED. Upstream tracks
# 12 files in its equivalent `.pi/` for exactly this reason. A blanket ignore
# would silently make the whole directory unaddable after the Task 0.3 rename.
# Ignore ephemeral state inside it by path, the way upstream does, and nothing
# more. The user's global state lives at `~/.apex-code/`, outside any repo.
.apex-code/hf-sessions/
.apex-code/hf-sessions-backup/
.apex-code_config/
apex-code-*.html

# Secrets — never commit. See AGENTS.md § Secrets.
.env.*
